RF.put("questb:b13",{"8493":{"id":8493,"t":"The Alliance Needs More Copper Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 copper bars to Sergeant Stonebrow at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\n20 Copper Bar","desc":"Back again ‹class›? Outstanding! We still need more stacks of copper bars if you can procure them for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort. Will you help us out?","rew":"You will receive:\nAlliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Back again, ‹class›? Outstanding! The bars you've provided thus far are really going to help out in making all sorts of things for the war. I know, for example, that the copper is going to be used for parts of the steam tanks that are being built, as well as in a small fleet of gyrocopters that we're planning to deploy if time allows.\nDon't let the stacks here fool you though, we still need more copper bars if you can procure them for the Ahn'Qiraj war effort. Will you help us out?","done":"Excellent work! Digging around for that copper and smelting it must have been quite an adventure. Unless you bought them at the auction house. Either way, it works for me. You are to be commended for your contribution to the war effort, ‹class›. And please don't hesitate to bring me more copper bars if you have them.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.4,"y":31.9,"n":"Sergeant Stonebrow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"653":{"id":653,"t":"Myzrael's Allies","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge.","desc":"<Myzrael speaks.>\nFree! I AM FREE! I am free to gather strength, hidden from my captors. For if they faced me now they would surely overpower and again imprison me.\nBut in time I will confront the giants, and they will regret their wardship of me!\nYou are a noble ally, ‹name›. I will need your help again in time. When I am ready, I will need you to summon me to the surface.\nSpeak with Gerrig Bonegrip. He is in Ironforge, in a shop of the Forlorn Cavern. He knows how I can be summoned.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","done":"The Lady told me of your coming, ‹class›. You are welcome in my abode for you, like I, serve a higher cause.\nArathi Highlands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":36.1,"y":58.1,"n":"Keystone","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Gerrig Bonegrip","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"733":{"id":733,"t":"Scrounging","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get 7 pieces of Scrap Metal for Sigrun.\n7 Scrap Metal Dustbelcher Warrior 50 % , Dustbelcher Mystic 50 % , Dustbelcher Brute 50 % , Dustbelcher Lord 38 % and 4 more","desc":"It's going to be tough going here if I can't manage to scrounge up some materials to construct some defenses and other necessities. I've noticed that the ogres in the area seem to be well equipped with scrap metal. Maybe the stories of siege engines in the Badlands weren't so far off after all...\nAnyways, the Prospector's been getting worried about the state of our little camp, so I'd like to get working soon if I can.\nThe main ogre camp is at Dustbelch Grotto, a good trek to the west of here.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSalbac Shield Ironheel Boots\nExperience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Well, I've made do with what I could, but... it's not much. Have you found any more supplies?","done":"It's a start, ‹name›, and it'll have to do until we hear word from Ironforge or the Explorers' League.\nNow, if only I could find some salt somewhere for my quenching barrel...","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":53.8,"y":43.3,"n":"Sigrun Ironhew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"97933":{"id":97933,"t":"Camping 101 herbalism","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Komin Winterhoof in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your herbalism skill to 20","desc":"Looks to me like you've gained some skill in herbalism. Picking flowers isn't just for dilly-dallying, you know. It can be useful... and profitable.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Incense Candle for your camp. High spirits are a key component to keeping healers and spellcasters in the fight, and an Incense Candle can provide a boost that magic users will surely appreciate.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Incense Candle. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":49.8,"y":39.8,"n":"Komin Winterhoof","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94253":{"id":94253,"t":"Craftsmans writ colorful kilt","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Colorful Kilt\nColorful Kilt","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Colorful Kilt, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Keep ya' head down, mon! Dey be watching...","done":"I plan to be sneakin' into the gates of Zul'Gurub soon, but I need the gear to blend in. Thinkin' I gear up like one of their ritualists.\nThis colorful kilt is exactly what I be needin'.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":50.6,"y":19.2,"n":"Hekshi","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94333":{"id":94333,"t":"Craftsmans writ ebon shiv","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Ebon Shiv\nEbon Shiv","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Ebon Shiv, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Ebon Shiv Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94333","cats":["crafting"]},"7933":{"id":7933,"t":"40 Tickets - Greater Darkmoon Prize","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Item #19182","rew":"You will receive:\nGreater Darkmoon Prize","back":"Step right up, step right up! If you have tickets from the Darkmoon Faire you'd like redeemed, then just say so! You can redeem tickets in various denominations for wondrous and fantastic prizes. Don't be shy, give it a try!\nItem #19182 (40)","done":"Here you go, here you go! A prize fit for a king! Congratulations to you, my friend!\nIf you have more tickets you'd like to turn in, then please let me know! For as long as the Darkmoon Faire is here, I'll redeem your tickets.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.2,"y":44.7,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.5,"y":68.9,"n":"Gelvas Grimegate","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"4813":{"id":4813,"t":"The Fragments Within","lv":14,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report back what you have found to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.","desc":"The moonwell water has revealed that embedded inside the crystal are a few small fragments of bone, as well as half of a jawbone. The jawbone appears to be from a humanoid, but it is unclear without breaking open the crystal - a feat that even the strongest of magic would find near impossible.\nWith the task at hand complete, all that remains is to report back to Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea in Auberdine.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBriarsteel Shortsword Curvewood Dagger Oakthrush Staff\nExperience: 975\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Well, it would seem that even though we know more about this crystal, more unanswered questions are the result!\nI'll take the information you've uncovered to the council here in Auberdine. Perhaps they'll know a course of action to follow on this crystal. Well, that is if there is one to be taken; for now, the threat remains far enough to our east to be out of harm's way.\nAs for you, please have this. Consider it a reward for a job well done, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":47.3,"y":48.7,"n":"Mysterious Red Crystal","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.7,"y":43.4,"n":"Sentinel Glynda Nal'Shea","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"4733":{"id":4733,"t":"Beached Sea Creature","lv":19,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sea Creature Bones to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Creature Bones Beached Sea Creature\nProvided: Sea Creature Bones","desc":"The remains of what appear to be a giant thresher have washed ashore on the rocky inlet of the Twilight Shore. The thresher is several times larger than any of the other threshers spotted in these parts. Wherever it came from, this creature would not seem to have been native to Darkshore.\nThough the creature has been picked apart in places, enough of it remains to gather a suitable sample for Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 725\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Thanks be to Elune - I am glad to see you again, dear ‹name›. The Temple of the Moon's work on the strange beaching phenomena continues here in Darkshore. Might you have anything additional to offer us?","done":"The dimensions of the thresher you mention are mind-boggling. Even the eldest of the threshers in this region grow to only a fraction of that size. While some larger ones were known to be close to Teldrassil, their numbers have declined steadily. I cannot help but wonder if these creatures beaching themselves here are somehow related to this.\nWhile we analyze the bones you have brought us, please accept this on behalf of the Temple of the Moon. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":31.3,"y":87.4,"n":"Beached Sea Creature","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1133":{"id":1133,"t":"Journey to Astranaar","lv":20,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shindrell Swiftfire in Astranaar.","desc":"If you're fresh off the boat from Menethil, then the first thing you should do is... go to Astranaar. I'm sure an eager member of the Alliance such as you can do some real good there. Speak with Shindrell Swiftfire and offer your services.\nBut don't bother mentioning who sent you. Shindrell does not know me...","rew":"Experience: 575","done":"You are here to offer your services to the Alliance, ‹name›? We welcome the aid, for although its beauty remains... Ashenvale Forest is not the peaceful place it once was.\nDustwallow Marsh Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.5,"y":45.1,"n":"Fiora Longears","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.7,"y":48.8,"n":"Shindrell Swiftfire","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98013":{"id":98013,"t":"Swelling forces","lv":20,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Eliminate 12 Stormscale Myrmidons, 8 Stormscale Sorceresses, and 6 Stormscale Warriors for Arbal at the Grove of the Ancients.\nStormscale Myrmidon slain : 0/ 12\nStormscale Sorceress slain : 0/ 8\nStormscale Warrior slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Steel yourself for your time in the ruins, young one... you will not be granted free passage there.\nScores of cursed Highborne, now known as naga, roam the once great city. Travel northeast and dispatch them from this land.\nWhat they once were... is no more. If they aid the Twilight's Hammer, they can bring only further pain to the forests that once gave them shelter.\nWar is what they seek, ‹class›. War... is what we will bring.","done":"Do not fret, young one. To pillage one's own home for some dark master...\nIt is unforgivable.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":43.6,"y":76.4,"n":"Arbal","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"973":{"id":973,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":24,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome to Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post.\nIlkrud Magthrull's Tome Ilkrud Magthrull","desc":"Ilkrud Magthrull. Yes, I have knowledge of him. He is a powerful orc warlock that makes his residence at the Fire Scar Shrine, a place of great evil in southwestern Ashenvale.\nHe had been little more than an annoyance until now, and I had not dealt with him, but it seems that his time has come.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nClergy Ring Staff of the Purifier\nExperience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You look a bit shaken up, ‹name›. Are you well?","done":"It was a grand thing you did today, ‹name›. You should be quite proud of yourself for having faced down a warlock of such power.\nNow, let's see what we can learn from Ilkrud's writings.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98893":{"id":98893,"t":"Conflict at darkspear islands","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.\nGo, show them the might of the horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Raiders\nLevel 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 98893","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"4493":{"id":4493,"t":"March of the Silithid","lv":53,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Alchemist Pestlezugg in Gadgetzan.","desc":"It would seem that the silithid's intent, nay - reason for being, is to devour everything in their path that is not of their ecology. Their focus is singular, and it is for this reason they are a grave threat to all life on Azeroth.\nWhat we've seen to date is but the first stages. I suspect that their strength comes from deeper in Kalimdor: Un'Goro Crater. Go to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak to Alchemist Pestlezugg. Tell him of my theory; he will surely aid us in fighting the silithid.","rew":"Experience: 525\n+10 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Yes, I gathered that Gracina sent you to me. Your experience in fighting these beasties is priceless; no one to my knowledge has ever dealt with their kind before. As for Gracina's idea that Un'Goro Crater is their heart... perhaps it is. Un'Goro is a mysterious and dangerous jungle to the west of here. Perhaps it is also one step closer to figuring out what the silithid are all about.\nDarnassus Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":41.8,"y":85.6,"n":"Gracina Spiritmight","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1373":{"id":1373,"t":"Ongeku","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Draenethyst Shard to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nDraenethyst Shard Ongeku\nReach 3000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"You have more to prove, and your next task will take you far, so for now the Gelkis will fight the Magram without you.\nThe earth whispers many secrets to those who listen. One secret I hear is of a red crystal. It is called draenethyst, and it is new to our earth. It comes from a place where mountains fly, and where demons rule.\nBring me a shard of draenethyst, and it will make my magic strong! The shard is in a place called the Swamp of Sorrows, held by the lost one Ongeku.","rew":"Experience: 2,850","back":"Show me you are a friend of the Gelkis, ‹name›.","done":"Yes, this is the shard of which the earth whispered. I can feel strong magic in it! I will use this magic against the enemies of the Gelkis.\nYou have done one more task for us, ‹name›. Maybe soon, we will call you friend.\nDesolace Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":36.2,"y":79.2,"n":"Uthek the Wise","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"9053":{"id":9053,"t":"A Better Ingredient","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve a Putrid Vine from the guardian at the bottom of the Sunken Temple and return to Torwa Pathfinder.\nPutrid Vine Atal'alarion","desc":"It is as I feared -- the toxin is simply too weak for such a powerful creature.\nIf we are to create a toxin of high enough potency, you must venture to the bottom of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar, unlock the secrets of the altar and recover a putrid vine from the guardian there. The temple is dangerous, and it would behoove you to bring friends.\nReturn to me when this is done.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrizzled Pelt Forest's Embrace Moonshadow Stave\nExperience: 6,350","back":"Have you recovered the vine?","done":"At last, the toxin can be created in full. I dare not require you to inflict it upon the creature again, as I have asked too much already.\nYou have my thanks and respect. May you be well in your travels, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"413":{"id":413,"t":"Shimmer Stout","lv":10,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Barrel of Shimmer Stout to Mountaineer Barleybrew.\nBarrel of Shimmer Stout\nProvided: Barrel of Shimmer Stout","desc":"I'd like my brother Wellart to try my new Shimmer Stout. He's a Mountaineer stationed in the southern guard tower, one of two towers on the border to Loch Modan.\nHe may not be a brewer like the rest of us Barleybrews, but he loves his drinks and I know he'll like this one.\nCan you bring him this Barrel of Shimmer Stout for me?","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Ironforge\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Hello, ‹class›! And what business takes you all the way out here?\nSomething exciting, I hope. I haven't been in a good fight in days, and this barrel of ale is almost dry...","done":"<Mountaineer Barleybrew tastes the Shimmer Stout...>\nOh. Whoa! This stuff really puts a shine in your eyes. I feel like I can see in the dark!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.7,"n":"Rejold Barleybrew","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":86.3,"y":48.8,"n":"Mountaineer Barleybrew","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"95213":{"id":95213,"t":"Stolen blasting powder","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Empty Powder Keg to Quarrymaster Thesten at Gol'Bolar Quarry.\nEmpty Powder Keg","desc":"The keg is stamped:\nBLASTING POWDER - DANGER - DO NOT HANDLE - DANGER - QUARRYMASTER AUTHORIZATION ONLY - DANGER\nYou get a sinking feeling that the troggs shouldn't have this. It would be best to report this to the quarry sooner rather than later.","back":"What's that you've got?","done":"<The ‹race› turns pale as he sees the empty keg.>\n...Where did you find this?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":69,"y":54.8,"n":"Quarrymaster Thesten","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"813":{"id":813,"t":"Finding the Antidote","lv":9,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Venomtail Poison Sacs to Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar.\n4 Venomtail Poison Sac Venomtail Scorpid 40 % , Corrupted Scorpid 40 % , Death Flayer 40 %","desc":"Venomtails are some of the deadliest scorpids in Durotar. It was unwise for Rhinag to hunt them without having some of the antidote with him, but right now, chastising is the last thing he needs.\nBring me a few venomtail poison sacs from any of the venomtails near the entrance of Orgrimmar and I'll make an antidote for him.\nMake haste, ‹name›. One of our own needs your help.","rew":"You will receive:\nVenomtail Antidote","back":"Remember, no matter what creature you hunt, you would do well to study it and understand its behavior. That knowledge could save your life.","done":"Here is the antidote, ‹name›. Take it to Rhinag as soon as you can, and be cautious.\nOrgrimmar Durotar","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":47.2,"y":53.6,"n":"Kor'ghan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"93":{"id":93,"t":"Dusky Crab Cakes","lv":20,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 6 Gooey Spider Legs and bring them to Chef Grual in Darkshire.\n6 Gooey Spider Leg Giant Plains Creeper 47.6 % , Plains Creeper 45 % , Elder Moss Creeper 41.7 % , Naraxis 39.6 % and 4 more","desc":"I'll let you in on a little secret - Dusky \"Crab\" Cakes are really made from spider legs! I know it's a bit disgusting, but the cakes have a nice, tangy flavor and make great snacks! Bring me Gooey Spider Legs and I'll whip you up a few of them.\nI hear Venom Web Spiders are a good source - they nest to the north, between the foothills and the river.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Gooey Spider Cake\nExperience: 775\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hail, ‹name›. Did you get those Gooey Spider Legs yet?","done":"Ah yes, a nice clutch of legs you have there! Let me just get these seasoned with my secret spices (no looking!) and get them to skittering on a skillet for a while...\nAnd, although Dusky Crab Cakes are my specialty and I won't give out the recipe, here's the recipe for a dish that's almost as good.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Chef Grual","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"173":{"id":173,"t":"Worgen in the Woods","lv":28,"min":23,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Nightbane Shadow Weaver worgen for Calor in Darkshire.\nNightbane Shadow Weaver slain : 0/ 6","desc":"Darkness seems drawn inexorably to Duskwood. Master Carevin's quest is the expulsion of evil and heresy. Through our efforts are the people of Darkshire kept safe.\nYou believe yourself worthy to join us?\nI once thought as you. Disillusioned by the complacency of the Watch, I joined Master Carevin. If you wish to prove yourself, it will not be through words.\nTest your skills against the Nightbane Shadow Weaver worgen in Brightwood Grove--bright, hah!--and the Rotting Orchard.","rew":"Money: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, how fares the hunt?","done":"Impressive, ‹name›. It would seem that you are capable enough to handle yourself. Perhaps a more suitable challenge could be found for one of your abilities.\nIt is curious though... The worgen seemed to just appear out of thin air. But then, with all the other strange creatures that have moved across our borders, I suppose it's only one of many concerns.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":47.6,"n":"Calor","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"253":{"id":253,"t":"Bride of the Embalmer","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Darkshire Shoulderguards.","obj":"Find Eliza's grave. Retrieve the Embalmer's Heart from her, then return to Ello Ebonlocke.\nThe Embalmer's Heart Eliza","desc":"The Embalmer is a name told in one of our children's stories. He was a kindly alchemist, driven mad by the death of his wife, Eliza. To restore her, he used dark magic to place his own heart within the bosom of his dead spouse.\nThis revived Eliza...but it cursed her with a hunger for human flesh, forcing the Embalmer to keep her buried.\nHis heart is his power. Find his wife's grave, retrieve his heart, and bring it to me while it still beats. Do this and his power will be broken.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMantle of Honor Darkshire Shoulderguards\nNew in Forever: Darkshire Shoulderguards.\nYou will also receive:\nCrest of Darkshire\nExperience: 3,650\n+200 reputation with Alliance","back":"Have you yet found Eliza's grave? Do you have the Embalmer's heart?","done":"You've done it! The magic within his heart will be proof against the Embalmer's evil, and a powerful aegis over the town of Darkshire.\nYou have done a great thing for our people, ‹name›. Your name will remain in our annals forever.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":71.9,"y":46.4,"n":"Lord Ello Ebonlocke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9213":{"id":9213,"t":"The Shadow Guard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -30g instead of 0.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 10 Insignia of the Crusade and 30 gold.\n10 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"A creation of genius! Much like the Ice Guard, the Shadow Guard employs a thin sheen of protective magic that covers certain pieces of equipment. And like the Ice Guard, the Shadow Guard is going to cost you a good amount of money.\n<Mataus holds his hand out and rubs his fingers together.>\nInterested?","rew":"You will receive:\nShadow Guard\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"<Mataus yawns.>\nBe gone, insect, lest you have something for me.","done":"<Mataus stuffs the gold into his robe.>\nWhat are you still standing around for, ‹race›? Our business is done.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"2973":{"id":2973,"t":"A New Cloak's Sheen","lv":45,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Iridescent Sprite Darter Wings to Krueg Skullsplitter in Camp Mojache.\n10 Iridescent Sprite Darter Wing Sprite Darter 19 % , Captured Sprite Darter 19 %","desc":"Well met, ‹class›. I've traveled with my companions down to the Feralas on a mission for our Orgrimmar masters.\nMy life-mate Korrin finds great pleasure in new clothing, so I aim to make her a new cloak adorned with the gossamer wings of faerie dragons. Would you be able to help me? Sprite darters with gorgeous wings I want are west of Camp Mojache.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The sprite darters can be dangerous critters when provoked. Be careful when dealing with them, ‹class›. And be even more careful of any night elves in the area. The pestering fools tend to hold up in the forests also.\nWhen you've gotten enough of the wings, let me know, I'll be sure to reward you well!","done":"Wonderful, ‹class›! These will do nicely. There are enough here to make a cloak for Korrin, and possibly even more! Thank you.\nI hope the trip wasn't too dangerous? The area of Feralas is not known for being forgiving, but you've obviously done well enough.\nThank you again, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":75.9,"y":42.7,"n":"Krueg Skullsplitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"94013":{"id":94013,"t":"Taming the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Vuldren Alpha in the Gustberry Lowlands. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.\nTame a Vuldren\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"You've returned triumphant from taming two beasts, it's time now for your last trial. The winds of Zephras whisper of greater challenges ahead.\nTake this Taming Rod and journey to the Gustberry Lowlands. There, tame a Vuldren Alpha and prove your mastery.\nComplete this lesson and you'll be ready to learn the deeper ways of the hunter.","back":"You will learn, Naanariel, and one day you will be a great ‹class›.","done":"Excellent, Naanariel! You are quite a fast learner. Now that you know the basics, I can teach you how to forge a lasting bond with an animal companion.\nGo with this knowledge and thrive. Be the ‹class› that Zephras Isle needs you to be.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59.6,"y":72.6,"n":"Quel'ana Quickgale","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"1453":{"id":1453,"t":"Reclaimers' Business in Desolace","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Kreldig Ungor in Desolace.","desc":"There's work to be done in Desolace, ‹name›. It's an atrocious place, befouled by centaur and other nasties. But if you're looking for a good week's honest work, then head there, meet with Kreldig Ungor, and tell him I sentcha.\nYou can find him holed up at Nijel's Point--it's a little cozy camp hidden in the mountains of northern Desolace. Just head east if you enter from the Stonetalon Mountains. It's easy to miss, so be on the lookout.","rew":"Experience: 1,300\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Glad to see the Reclaimers aren't in short supply of work, or adventurers willing to help out.\nI'm Kreldig, ‹name›. You've made a smart move helpin' out the Reclaimers. Everyone needs something these days: they've lost a family heirloom, a magic item, a loved one. You never can tell. But with the Reclaimers around, there's no reason, for the right price, everyone can't find what they've lost.\nDun Morogh Desolace","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":24.5,"n":"Roetten Stonehammer","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":66.2,"y":9.6,"n":"Kreldig Ungor","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8653":{"id":8653,"t":"Goldwell the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":46.7,"y":51.6,"n":"Elder Goldwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8253":{"id":8253,"t":"Destroy Morphaz","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Arcane Shard from Morphaz and return to Archmage Xylem.\nArcane Shard Morphaz","desc":"There is a green drake deep in the sunken temple of Atal'Hakkar by the name of Morphaz.\nYears ago, he overwhelmed me in a bold ambush and consumed my apprentice whole. While the loss of an apprentice is not unknown to me, this particular one carried an arcane shard of unsurpassed size and quality.\nYou must gather powerful allies and delve into the temple. Destroy Morphaz and recover the arcane shard from his ageless stomach.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGlacial Spike Arcane Crystal Pendant Fire Ruby\nMoney: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,350","back":"Have you slain my old nemesis?","done":"Incredible. The shard has grown as it absorbed the drake's energy over the long years.\nThere is no more I can ask of you now. My full ability to forge the arcane has returned with this shard. My first creation is yours, ‹name›, and you have but to choose...","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":29.2,"y":40.2,"n":"Archmage Xylem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"8813":{"id":8813,"t":"One Commendation Signet","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"For those adventurers who have but a single commendation signet, I'll exchange it for a small amount of recognition with Darnassus.\nPlease bear in mind that it is better to hand over a stack of ten signets at once; your efforts will receive greater recognition in doing so. We offer a single signet exchange as a service for those who don't have enough for a full stack of ten.\nWith that being said, I stand ready to assist you if you still wish to hand in a single signet.","done":"Very well - your deeds have been entered into the records, and you are duly recognized for your efforts. Keep up the good work, ‹class›.\nIf you have any more signets to hand in, then I am able to assist you further in that regard.\nDun Morogh Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.9,"y":33.4,"n":"Ironforge Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Lunalight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"1053":{"id":1053,"t":"In the Name of the Light","lv":40,"min":34,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey and then report back to Raleigh the Devout in Southshore.\nHigh Inquisitor Whitemane slain in Scarlet Monastery\nScarlet Commander Mograine slain in Scarlet Monastery\nHerod slain in Scarlet Monastery\nHoundmaster Loksey slain in Scarlet Monastery","desc":"I once served the Scarlet Crusade with honor, loyalty and pride. I believed their cause to be a noble one: to rid Azeroth of the undead.\nBut as I spent time at the Monastery in Tirisfal Glades I realized that their grasp on reality was slipping. They now think everyone is plagued who doesn't wear the tabard of the Crusade. Innocent men and women were tortured because they were supposedly plagued.\nThe Scarlet Crusade must be crushed in the name of the Light. You, ‹name›, must destroy the deranged regime.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSword of Serenity Bonebiter Black Menace Orb of Lorica\nExperience: 4,700\n+200 reputation with Stormwind","back":"The corruption in the Monastery will not end until the highest ranking officials have been removed.\nIn the name of the Light, slay High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey. Once they have fallen, perhaps the true cause can be rekindled. Until then, anyone who crosses the path of the Crusade lies in peril.\nVenture forth from Southshore and make it so!","done":"While disciples of the Light never revel in the loss of life, we must accept that on occasion, such sacrifices must happen for the greater good of the Kingdom and the planet.\nThrough your deeds in the Monastery you have spared many innocent lives, ‹name›. I salute your tenacity.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":51.5,"y":58.4,"n":"Raleigh the Devout","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scarlet-monastery"]},"3453":{"id":3453,"t":"The Torch of Retribution","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Kalaran Windblade to complete the Torch of Retribution.","desc":"Give me a moment to combine the pieces and apply the necessary enchantments.","rew":"Experience: 470","back":"Do not interrupt the channeling process.","done":"There is one final task that you must complete.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39,"n":"Kalaran Windblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8413":{"id":8413,"t":"Da Voodoo","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the voodoo feathers to Bath'rah the Windwatcher.\n2 Amber Voodoo Feather Gasher , Zul'Lor\n2 Blue Voodoo Feather Hukku , Mijan\n2 Green Voodoo Feather Zolo , Loro","desc":"The spirit totem just isn't enough. We be needin' some voodoo magic to make it work jus' right.\nThe trolls in the sunken temple have feathers strong with voodoo magics. Go there and kill Gasher, Mijan, Zolo, Hukku, Zul'lor, and Loro. Then we have magic enough for a real spirit totem.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAzurite Fists Enamored Water Spirit Wildstaff\nMoney: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,350","back":"Where's the feathers, mon?","done":"It's about time this troll got a full night's rest! The spirit totem will watch over me.\nI been a long time collectin' things, maybe you want somethin' for all your trouble?","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"92893":{"id":92893,"t":"No mercy for the weak","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones. Return to Orgrul after the task is complete.\nGelkis Captive slain : 0/ 5\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"As you tread further into the Valley of Bones, you will find Gelkis wanderers that dared to enter our territory. I instructed they be kept alive so they could feed the bone worms burrowing about, but they seem uninterested in their prey being alive.\nThis task is simple. Find the prisoners, then snuff out their life. Don't give them a brief glimmer of hope for freedom.\nShen'dralas Open the zone on the world map Level 42 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 38 40 45 53 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 92893\nThe chain\n14 quests from level 32 to 43, 34,280 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] Bristleback Retreat\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and slay quilboar at Bristleback Retreat.\n3,600 XP\n11 [ 43 ] Long-Term Solutions\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram clan and slay 2 Outc","cats":["shendralas"]},"8573":{"id":8573,"t":"Champion's Battlegear","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Cenarion Combat Badges, 20 Cenarion Logistics Badges, 20 Cenarion Tactical Badges and 1 Mark of Cenarius to Vargus at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to be able to complete this quest.\n15 Cenarion Combat Badge\n20 Cenarion Logistics Badge\n20 Cenarion Tactical Badge\nMark of Cenarius\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The badges you collect from performing combat, logistics and tactical assignments for Cenarion Hold are more than just for show, ‹name›.\nYou'd be wise to hold on to them. As you prove your loyalty to our organization I can offer you some of the gear we reserve for our closest allies in exchange for those badges.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFist of Cenarius Wrath of Cenarius Earthstrike\nExperience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"It's in our best interest to keep our most loyal allies well geared, ‹name›.","done":"Great work, ‹name›. Please accept this on behalf of the Cenarion Circle. You've certainly earned it, friend!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.9,"n":"Vargus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8333":{"id":8333,"t":"Medallion of Station","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Large Brilliant Shard\n3 Abyssal Crest Crimson Templar , Azure Templar , Hoary Templar , Earthen Templar","rew":"You will receive:\nTwilight Cultist Medallion of Station\nExperience: 6,600","back":"If you need another Twilight cultist's medallion of station, then I am happy to oblige. I will, however, need another brilliant shard and some abyssal crests...","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. One more Twilight medallion of station. Use it well, and I wish you luck against the Abyssal Council!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"493":{"id":493,"t":"Journey to Hillsbrad Foothills","lv":20,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Apothecary Renferrel's findings to Apothecary Lydon in the town of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills.\nRenferrel's Findings\nProvided: Renferrel's Findings","desc":"The Royal Apothecary Society is under extreme pressure from the Dark Lady to develop a New Plague. We are working diligently and have made much progress. It is our belief that the success will be achieved much faster if we share information amongst the Society.\nFor that reason I want you to deliver my latest findings to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, a small town nestled in the Hillsbrad Foothills. The journey will be a long one.\nHead south and stick to the roads. Follow the signs closely!","rew":"Money: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"You have something for me?","done":"Ah, most excellent. Apothecary Renferrel has my utmost respect. I am anxious to study his work.\nSilverpine Forest Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":42.8,"y":40.9,"n":"Apothecary Renferrel","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"333":{"id":333,"t":"Harlan Needs a Resupply","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Canal Tailor Shop and bring Rema Schneider the Cloth Request from Harlan Bagley.\nCloth Request\nProvided: Cloth Request","desc":"We've been doing a lot of business lately. It seems like everyone is buying armor and sturdy clothes. Almost like they expect a cold, harsh season ahead...\nBut those are future worries. My worry today is that I'm running out of knitted clothing to sell. I need another load from our supplier.\nIf you can take this request to Rema Schneider at the Canal Tailor and Fit Shop, I'd be most grateful.","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 0 silver, 17 copper Experience: 85\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You bring word from Mr. Bagley?","done":"It says here that Harlan's business is booming. That's good news, but I wonder why people have need of all that armor. I've heard nothing of open war... is there something the nobles aren't telling us?\nWell, thank you for bringing the request. Here's your payment, and I'll see to it that Harlan gets his supplies.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":62.3,"y":67.9,"n":"Harlan Bagley","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":58.1,"y":67.5,"n":"Rema Schneider","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"95773":{"id":95773,"t":"Enemies in the water","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gather 10 Brinescale Tridents from Brinescale Skirmishers.\n10 Brinescale Trident","desc":"‹class›, your arrival is timely. I have just received new reports of naga activity just off of our coast. They seem to be swarming around some old troll ruins near the ocean floor.\nWe are already stretched thin defending from the local Bloodscalp and ogres ransacking our caravans. We cannot afford a surprise attack from the sea.\nGo and slay as many as you are able, and bring me their tridents as proof of your success.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar\nStranglethorn Vale Open the zone on the world map Level 37 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 33 35 40 47 Side Horde Shareable Yes Quest ID 95773","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"573":{"id":573,"t":"Mok'thardin's Enchantment","lv":44,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Far Seer Mok'thardin of Grom'gol needs Holy Spring Water. He also wants you to kill 10 Naga Explorers.\nHoly Spring Water The Holy Spring\nNaga Explorer slain : 0/ 10","desc":"There is but one final reagent needed to complete the enchantment.\nIn the south, towards the western coast, high above the bluffs, lies a Holy Spring. This spring is the subject of great conflict amongst religious and mystical scholars. Every race in Azeroth claims that the spring waters were made divine for their people.\nMy final request of you: bring to me Holy Spring Water. Be warned. An expedition of naga explorers have advanced upon the spring. They will need to be dealt with as well.","rew":"You will receive:\nChoker of the High Shaman\nExperience: 4,650\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I am almost ready to complete the enchantment. Have you performed my bidding?","done":"With this Holy Spring Water the ceremonial choker is ready for enchantment.\nWear this with pride, ‹name›, in the name of the Warchief and in defense of the mighty Horde.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.1,"y":29.2,"n":"Far Seer Mok'thardin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5213":{"id":5213,"t":"The Active Agent","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,850, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme and search the ziggurats. Find and return new Scourge Data to Betina Bigglezink.\nScourge Data Scourge Data in Stratholme","desc":"You will have to delve deeper into Stratholme, ‹name›.\nBeyond the first gates you will find the ziggurats. We know that the Scourge draws great power from these structures. Search the Ziggurats and return with any information that you may discover.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSeal of the Dawn Rune of the Dawn\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"We are on the verge of discovering what this new active plague agent may be!","done":"Astonishing! This will take months to dissect and analyze. The Argent Dawn thanks you for your efforts, ‹name›.\nWith our blessing, take your pick between either this Seal of the Dawn or this Rune of the Dawn. You can use either of them instead of a standard Argent Dawn Commission to collect scourgestones on our behalf. Should you lose yours, speak with me and I'll get you a replacement.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":49.9,"n":"Betina Bigglezink","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"3373":{"id":3373,"t":"The Essence of Eranikus","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Place the Essence of Eranikus in the Essence Font located in this lair in the Sunken Temple.\nEssence of Eranikus Shade of Eranikus\nProvided: Essence of Eranikus","desc":"As you touch the gem, a deep voice resonates in your mind.\n\"Mortal, heed this plea. I am Eranikus of the Green Dragonflight, keeper of this accursed temple. My charge to ensure that the trolls never again bring forth their abomination of a god has for now ended in failure. As I imbue this gem with part of my essence, I sense my grip on the Dream twisting into chaos. Please - place this gem into the essence font in my lair, and let our magic there purge the taint from my psyche so that I may rest.\"","rew":"You will receive:\nChained Essence of Eranikus\nExperience: 2,800","back":"As you near the essence font that Eranikus told you of, his voice once again touches your mind.\n\"Yes mortal, this essence font will redeem what untainted element of my psyche remains imbued in this gem. Place the gem inside the font, and let the magic of the Green Dragonflight cleanse the corruption and taint from my being. Only then will I find true release, and only then will the Dragonflight be able to reassert their stewardship over the Atal'ai.\"","done":"You place the gem inside the essence font.\n\"Thank you mortal, you have - no... this, this cannot be! No! The corruption of this accursed god even taints the sanctity of a Green Dragonflight essence font! No please, I feel my essence ripping from me! THE PAIN! I feel the grip of an eternal nightmare taking hold on me...\"\n\"Mortal, I implore you! Find one of the Green Dragonflight to stop this... help me... I am chained in darkness... forever in agony... please do not torture...\"\nStart an item: Essence of Eranikus End Essence Font Level 55 , requires level 48 Difficulty 48 51 53 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 3373\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 55, 7,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 55 ] The Essence of Eranikus this quest\nPlace the Essence of Eranikus in the Essence Font located in this lair in the Sunken Temple.\nEssence of Eranikus\n2,800 XP\n2 [ 55 ] The Essence of Eranikus\nBring the Oathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight and the Chained Essence of Eranikus to Itharius in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nOathstone of Ysera's Dragonflight\n550 XP\n3 [ 55 ] In Eranikus' Own Words\nTravel to the eastern part of Winterspring and speak with Umbranse the Spiritspeaker.\nItharius Swamp of Sorrows\n4,200 XP","cats":["sunken-temple"]},"8733":{"id":8733,"t":"Eranikus, Tyrant of the Dream","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the continent of Teldrassil and find Malfurion's agent somewhere outside the walls of Darnassus.","desc":"This is a journey of redemption, hero. Would it be that I was slain today, I would have died for a just and righteous cause. You must recover the green scepter shard. You must cleanse Eranikus of the taint placed upon him by the Old Gods.\nTravel to Darnassus. Just outside the city walls you will find one of my agents. This agent will set things in motion for us and inform Tyrande of our plans without alerting Staghelm.\n<Malfurion sighs.>\nA fall from grace a thousand years in the making...","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+25 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"The wisp is silent except for a low humming sound. Oddly enough, it is able to communicate with you through thoughts.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":37.6,"y":47.9,"n":"Forest Wisp","e":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"8893":{"id":8893,"t":"The Super Egg-O-Matic","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hippogryph Egg Hippogryph Egg","rew":"You will receive:\nEgg Crate","back":"The Super Egg-O-Matic is the latest of Curgle Cranklehop's inventions. It is quite an impressive piece of machinery.\nThe Super Egg-O-Matic sputters wildly as you approach the control panel.","done":"You place the hippogryph egg into the machine. A series of beeps follows along with some strange mechanical sounds.\nIt appears that the Eggometer has weighed, measured, and packaged your egg. Now that's speedy service!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.4,"y":27,"n":"Egg-O-Matic","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"99053":{"id":99053,"t":"Escaping banethil","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Help Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom escape Ban'ethil Barrow Den, and report her is safety to Sentinel Kyra Starsong in Dolanaar.\nEscort Lynessa Duskblossom out of Ban'ethil","desc":"My prayers have been answered! I am thankful that you have fought your way down here.\nI was sent here by the Oracle Tree to deliver a message to the slumbering druids here only to find it completely overrun by furbolg! They ambushed me before I could turn back and brought me down here--I fear for their next meal.\nI don't know about you, but I loathe this place. Under the earth is no place for the kaldorei.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBan'ethil Quiver Sentinel's Slasher","done":"Thank Elune you were around to help Lynessa avoid a dark fate with the Gnarlpine. She's one of our best, and a personal friend.\nPlease, take this in thanks. May it serve you well in keeping the kaldorei safe.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":44.6,"y":58.9,"n":"Sentinel Lynessa Duskblossom","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56,"y":59.4,"n":"Sentinel Kyra Starsong","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"98093":{"id":98093,"t":"Field to clear","lv":23,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sulhasa in southern Barrens wants you to clear out 7 Stormhide lizards and 7 Hecklefang Stalkers in the area so she can leave the tree safely.\nHecklefang Stalker slain : 0/ 7\nStormhide slain : 0/ 7","desc":"I'm so glad you saw me!\nThe weather was lovely this morning, so I walked from Camp Taurajo down the golden road. When it came time to head back, I couldn't--a pack of hyenas started circling, and Stormhide lizards blocked my only escape.\nScrambling up this tree I went, and now there are too many foes about at this hour for me to make the run home through the fields.\nWould you mind clearing out these Stormhide and Hecklefang Stalkers for me?","rew":"You will receive:\nTaurajo Headband\nExperience: 1,850\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Thank you for helping me out, Illbean. I'll let Camp Taurajo know you were able to rescue me. I'm so lucky you helped, I could have been stuck there all day!\nThis is all I have to spare, but I hope it's useful to you.\nI'll be making my exit once I make the careful climb down.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":47.8,"y":77.6,"n":"Sulhasa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"893":{"id":893,"t":"Weapons of Choice","lv":24,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Razormane Backstabber, a Charred Razormane Wand and a Razormane War Shield to Tatternack Steelforge at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.\nRazormane Backstabber Razormane Stalker 15 % , Razormane Pathfinder 15 %\nCharred Razormane Wand Razormane Seer 15 %\nRazormane War Shield Razormane Warfrenzy 15 %","desc":"The Razormane quilboars to the south, beyond the Field of Giants, have no skilled blacksmiths from what I am told, but they've apparently started to develop sturdier weapons. I'd like to get my hands on a few different types to learn their techniques if possible.\nIf you wish to help bring honor to the Horde, then bring me examples of their weapons. Find me a dagger from their stalkers, a wand from their seers, and a shield from their warfrenzy. That should do nicely!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDemolition Hammer Everglow Lantern\nExperience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I, too, have doubts that the pathetic quilboars could attain any level of skill in the area of smithing, but I do as the Warchief commands, and I shall learn what I can about the Razormane tribe.\nI have had more menial tasks, and I do so willingly if it aids the orc people.","done":"Excellent, excellent specimens indeed.\nThe quilboar are further along than I had expected.\nHere, ‹class›, take this and get out of my way. I'd better take a closer look at these weapons. We may have underestimated our enemy, and that's the kind of mistake we can't afford to make.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.1,"y":57.7,"n":"Tatternack Steelforge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1693":{"id":1693,"t":"Weapons of Elunite","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nElunite Axe Elunite Hammer Elunite Dagger Elunite Sword\nExperience: 625","done":"‹name›, I have crafted these weapons with the elunite you brought to me. Please, take whichever most suits you.\nAnd I must thank you. Working with elunite is both an honor and a pleasure.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":59.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Mathiel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5533":{"id":5533,"t":"Scholomance","lv":55,"min":55,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Alchemist Arbington at Chillwind Point, Western Plaguelands.","desc":"On the island of Caer Darrow lies Scholomance - a wretched center of Scourge necromancy and evil. Our enemy dwells within, conducting unspeakable acts of depravity on unwitting victims... at least, we surmise as much. A door bars the way, and try as we might no entry is to be had without a proper key.\nAlchemist Arbington is well versed on Scholomance, and has an idea how to obtain a key. You have proved your worth to me, and now I entrust this task to you. Speak with him on this matter.","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"Well met, ‹class›. I've dedicated a fair portion of my recent studies to the Scholomance, and I believe I know a means by which you can acquire a key... one that will let you past the front door.\nI can only imagine what horrid sights are to be seen inside, ‹name›. I don't know how you heroic types do it sometimes...","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":84,"n":"Commander Ashlam Valorfist","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42.7,"y":83.8,"n":"Alchemist Arbington","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"4973":{"id":4973,"t":"Counting Out Time","lv":56,"min":53,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Locate 5 Andorhal Watches amongst the rubble of the city, and return with them to Chromie in the Andorhal Inn, Western Plaguelands.\n5 Andorhal Watch Small Lockbox","desc":"If you are willing to help once more, I can certainly use your assistance. I'll gladly take more watches you might uncover from the ruins of Andorhal. They certainly help me in maintaining a balance against whatever malign force is meddling with the timeline here.\nIn exchange for those watches, I'll give you another item that, in the future, I suspect you'll find quite the use for.","rew":"You will receive:\nAttuned Dampener\nExperience: 575","back":"The watches of Andorhal, much like the large clock on the ruins of the town hall, all are frozen in time at three o'clock. This was when the full effects of the plague first spread out over the city, choking the life out of it.\nAs much as we all may regret what happened that day, it has shaped the flow of time as you mortals perceive it. The bronze dragonflight must persevere in protecting the timeline!","done":"Again, I think you for your assistance. Please accept this gift. While you still may not know when to use such an item, perhaps in the future the path of time will reveal its true intentions to you. You could say that I've seen as such happening to you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"13":{"id":13,"t":"The People's Militia","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gryan Stoutmantle wants you to kill 15 Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters and return to him on Sentinel Hill.\nDefias Pillager slain : 0/ 15\nDefias Looter slain : 0/ 15","desc":"A band of vicious Defias Pillagers has been seen plundering the Gold Coast Quarry, Moonbrook and the Alexston Farmstead. The People's Militia will not stand for such behavior. Dispatch immediately, ‹name›, and make the Light's presence known in Westfall.\nThe Gold Coast Quarry is near the shore, to the West of the tower. As the next step of your training, I want you to kill 15 of those foul Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters.","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"We have not time to talk, ‹name›. The Defias Pillagers are denying the people of Westfall the peace and prosperity they deserve. Make sure at least 15 Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters have been killed. That will send a clear message that corruption is not welcome here.","done":"Your worth to The People's Militia has been validated by your brave acts thus far.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.3,"y":47.5,"n":"Gryan Stoutmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"94413":{"id":94413,"t":"A magical affront","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 6 Windshaper Novice Seers in Shen'dar Highlands.\nWindshaper Novice Seer defeated : 0/ 6","desc":"The recent emergence of the ley lines on the surface of Zephras has been profound for our order. We have more direct and tangible access to the energies that permeate this place and it has increased our understanding of said magic greatly.\nThe Windshapers, however, view these emergences as scars on the land that must be \"healed\". This is an affront to our order and is something we simply cannot abide.\nGo to the ley line in the forest to the southwest and drive off the Windshapers you find there.","rew":"You will receive:\nDowsing Rod Elixir of Minor Strength\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 550\n+100 reputation with High Order","done":"Sometimes I find it hard to distinguish between the blind zealotry of the Al'Aketh cult, and the stubborn refusal of the Windshapers to change.\nIf they truly believed the winds would guide us, they should be sensing the direction the winds are blowing and flow with them rather than against them.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45,"y":46.4,"n":"Rathiril Sunlance","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94493":{"id":94493,"t":"A sacrifice in vain","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Elegael Thornpaw in the northeastern part of Shadowgale Forest.","desc":"Thank goodness our message got to Lotheluum. Wait, where are the rest of the reinforcements? Surely it is not just you they sent?\n<Elegael pales as you explain yourself.>\nSo the message did not get to Valanaar. We are in dire straights indeed then.\n<Elegael sighs deeply then looks resolute.>\nThen we must handle this on our own. Time is of the essence.","done":"The Al'aketh Cultists ambushed us with little to no warning. Many inside my den lay wounded or dying. I had attempted to send a message to Valanaar but it appears my efforts were in vain.\nPlease, if you have come here I beg for your help. I don't know how much longer my fellows will be able to survive this onslaught.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});